  "job": {
    "id": "demo-job",
    "title": "IT Systems Administrator (demo)",
    "jdText": "IT Systems Administrator\n\nAbout the role\nWe are a 250-person logistics company looking for an IT Systems Administrator to keep our offices, warehouse and remote staff running. You will own our Windows server estate, user accounts, network and end-user support, and work with a small IT team of three.\n\nWhat you will do\n- Administer Windows Server, Active Directory, Group Policy, DNS and DHCP.\n- Manage Microsoft 365 (Exchange Online, Teams, SharePoint) and user onboarding and offboarding.\n- Maintain the LAN/WAN, firewalls, switches, Wi-Fi and VPN; troubleshoot connectivity issues.\n- Run our VMware virtual environment, backups and disaster-recovery tests.\n- Act as the escalation point for help-desk tickets and keep our ticketing system and documentation up to date.\n- Patch and secure servers and endpoints; support security audits.\n\nRequirements\n- 3+ years of experience in systems administration or IT support.\n- Hands-on experience administering Windows Server and Active Directory.\n- Solid understanding of networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VLANs).\n- Experience supporting end users and resolving hardware and software issues.\n- Experience with virtualization (VMware or Hyper-V).\n- Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent experience.\n\nNice to have\n- CompTIA A+, Network+ or Security+, or a Microsoft certification.\n- Scripting with PowerShell to automate admin tasks.\n- Experience with cloud platforms (Azure or AWS).\n- Familiarity with ITIL practices.\n\nWe value clear communication and a calm approach to fixing problems under pressure.\n",
